A macro call naming a path no config tier declares fails with exit 2, naming the missing
path on stderr, and writes nothing.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md commit="{{ macro('core.macros.nope') }}"
-- exit --
2
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: value "{{ macro('core.macros.nope') }}": no macro declared at config path: core.macros.nope
